  "goodToKnow": "Die Inklusion means inclusion, especially of people with disabilities in society and schools: inklusiver Unterricht, where children with and without disabilities learn together. Germany ratified the UN Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities in 2009, and since then Inklusion has been a major, sometimes controversial school topic, because Germany traditionally had separate Förderschulen. Inklusiv also means including: inklusive Frühstück."
